# PINNED MISSING SET -- every cell of qa/method-inventory.json that is owed an implementation
# and does not have one. RECORDED ON PURPOSE, exactly as testing/a2a-tck/check-baseline.py pins the
# TCK's full per-requirement map: a suite whose result is UNCHANGING is still a gate, because the
# thing a gate has to catch is a CHANGE.
#
# crates/busbar/tests/method_coverage.rs asserts the computed MISSING set EQUALS this file, byte
# for byte, in both directions:
#
#   a cell that appears here and is now implemented  -> UNEXPECTED COVERAGE, red. Delete the line
#                                                       in the same commit that implements it, so
#                                                       the work queue shrinks visibly.
#   a cell that regresses into MISSING               -> red, because it is not listed here.
#
# So this file is the 1.6.0 work queue, and it is not possible to land a cell without editing it.
#
# THIS FILE IS NOT A WAIVER LIST. A line here says "owed and not built". A waiver says "not owed,
# and here is why" and lives in qa/method-coverage.status with a date and a reason. Do not move a
# line from here to there to make a number go green -- a documented security decision is never
# reversed to make a number go green, and neither is an undocumented gap laundered into a waiver.
#
# Regenerate deliberately (read the diff -- a new line is a new gap):
#   BUSBAR_PIN_MISSING_CELLS=1 cargo test -p busbar --test method_coverage
#
